(ADR-0002) Tj
T*
(ADR-0002 Control software architecture) Tj
T*
(Status: Accepted) Tj
T*
(Parts: VC-CT-6800, VC-CT-6810, VC-CT-6220, VC-HB-2100, VC-HB-2300, VC-ASM-5000) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# ADR-0002 - Control software architecture) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Status) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Stefan \(CTO\) accepted this decision on 2026-11-20.) Tj
T*
(The accepted rule is: "the right parts in the right language, clean and structured".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use Rust for time-critical code and for code next to the safety circuit.) Tj
T*
(Use Python only for tools.) Tj
T*
(Do not use CODESYS on this path.) Tj
T*
(Rust owns the cyclic loop and the machine state machine.) Tj
T*
(Rust owns the Modbus RTU master and the DIO process image.) Tj
T*
(Python owns test benches, data analysis, plm-sync and hardware-in-the-loop scripts.) Tj
T*
(The target cycle is 10 ms on a PREEMPT_RT kernel.) Tj
T*
(Run the control thread on one isolated core with policy SCHED_FIFO.) Tj
T*
(Call mlockall before the loop.) Tj
T*
(Use a software watchdog and the RevPi hardware watchdog.) Tj
T*
(Do not publish MQTT and do not build JSON on the loop thread.) Tj
T*
(Measure the cycle on a Connect 4 before you state a jitter value.) Tj
T*
(The state machine covers hub, sonic, sampling, tilt and faults.) Tj
T*
(Sampling is the hub drill sequence plus the lift deploy.) Tj
T*
(Keep the state codes from the Structured Text blocks.) Tj
T*
(The fault codes stay the table in ADR-0001.) Tj
T*
(Do not add a fault code.) Tj
T*
(The controller is RevPi Connect 4, part VC-CT-6800, plus one RevPi DIO, part VC-CT-6810.) Tj
T*
(The RevPi is the Modbus RTU master on the RS-485 port.) Tj
T*
(Use device node /dev/piControl0 with ioctl, read and write.) Tj
T*
(Byte offsets come from PiCtory and are not frozen.) Tj
T*
(The lift drive is SINAMICS S200 PTI order 6SL5510-1BB11-0AA0 \(VC-HB-2300\).) Tj
T*
(That drive is Modbus slave 2 and needs firmware V6.3 HF4 or later.) Tj
T*
(The S200 executes position control, the speed profile and the brake on X108.) Tj
T*
(The RevPi sends target values and reads status values.) Tj
T*
(The RevPi does not close the position loop.) Tj
T*
(The RevPi does not release the motor brake with a DIO output.) Tj
T*
(Position comes from the 1FL2 absolute encoder in part VC-HB-2100.) Tj
T*
(VC-HB-3410, the chain-shaft encoder, is obsolete.) Tj
T*
(There is no chain encoder, so do not buy VC-HB-3410.) Tj
T*
(The sonic-head inverter is slave 1 and its order code is not selected.) Tj
T*
(The sonic register map is TODO.) Tj
T*
(Register 40100 is the example control word, and 40101 is the speed setpoint.) Tj
T*
(Those two numbers are not verified on this drive.) Tj
T*
(Mark every unverified register as TODO.) Tj
T*
(Keep the safety function in the hard-wired circuit.) Tj
T*
(Wire Pilz PNOZ s4 article 750104 \(VC-CT-6220\) to S200 STO input X131.) Tj
T*
(The RevPi software only reads the feedback contacts.) Tj
T*
(The software can send a normal stop.) Tj
T*
(Do not credit the RevPi software in any ISO 13849 performance level.) Tj
T*
(A software crash must not be the only path that removes torque.) Tj
T*
(ADR-0001 is not changed.) Tj
T*
(Node-RED, MQTT and Modbus TCP remain the HMI path only.) Tj
T*
(Do not put a state machine in Node-RED.) Tj
T*
(The 60 tests in test_safety, test_hub, test_sonic and test_integration stay the reference.) Tj
T*
(Port the tests to Rust and keep a golden-vector harness.) Tj
T*
(The Python model and the Rust model must agree on each vector.) Tj
T*
(This change ports three safety tests as the pattern.) Tj
T*
(The workspace path is `firmware/revpi/`.) Tj
T*
(The crates are `vc-core`, `vc-io`, `vc-modbus` and `vc-runtime`.) Tj
T*
(`vc-core` has no device I/O and stays compatible with no_std where practical.) Tj
T*
(The full loop is not implemented.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Alternatives) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(CODESYS Control Basic M, article 2302000048, was considered.) Tj
T*
(The list price starts at 69 EUR excluding tax and is not a quote.) Tj
T*
(This decision rejects CODESYS.) Tj
T*
(The control loop is native Rust, not a soft PLC.) Tj
T*
(A demo licence stops after two hours.) Tj
T*
(Do not ship a demo licence on a field machine.) Tj
T*
(A Python cyclic service was considered.) Tj
T*
(This decision rejects Python for the cyclic loop.) Tj
T*
(Garbage collection can pause the process and can miss the 10 ms cycle.) Tj
T*
(Python remains the tool language.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Consequences) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Buy the RevPi Connect 4 and one RevPi DIO for this path.) Tj
T*
(Do not buy a CODESYS Basic M licence for this path.) Tj
T*
(Do not buy VC-HB-3410.) Tj
T*
(Confirm the S200 map on firmware V6.3 HF4 or later.) Tj
T*
(Select the sonic inverter before you fill its register map.) Tj
T*
(`CONTROL_SYSTEM.md` still describes the WAGO rack and is not changed here.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
